  "$comment": "Campaign level 17 (stretch 3): a river delta. Six islands linked by sand fords that two repeating tides drown and drain out of step. The Shaper takes the ford ward at the centre and keeps it for three minutes while both rivals wade over to pray it away (the war tribe always sends three fresh wardens, so the hold is contested; the bot loses the ward to them and only wins it back near tick 14500, which paces its win near 24150); then two ley stones seeded to the sneaky rival wake on the north island, and praying them away raises a permanent causeway; keep the ward and both stones for a minute, cross the causeway and burn the sneaky Hearth; that wakes a seer on the south island held by the war tribe behind posted wardens, and praying it away raises a second causeway; then break the war tribe (population capped at 70 so it neither snowballs into a stalemate nor collapses early).",
